From: Andrzej Rogozynski <sellen@cs-lab.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] m68k: fix DImode shift-by-32 push/pop splits with an sp-relative source

The pre_dec split of (ashift:DI x 32) pushes 0, then the low word of x;
the post_inc split of (lshiftrt:DI x 32) stores 0, then the high word.
When x is addressed through the auto-modified register (typically a
DImode spill slot pushed as a call argument: move.l 72(%sp),-(%sp) after
clr.l -(%sp)), the second move reads 4 bytes off, the other word of x.

Seen with -mcpu=68060 tuning in OpenSSL 3.3 (crypto/threads_pthread.c,
ossl_synchronize_rcu: __atomic_fetch_or_8 (..., (uint64_t) id << 32)
received 0 << 32, so the RCU writer waited forever for its id).

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
--- a/gcc/config/m68k/m68k.md	2026-10-15 01:43:17
+++ b/gcc/config/m68k/m68k.md	2026-10-15 01:43:17
@@ -4519,6 +4519,13 @@
 {
   operands[0] = adjust_address(operands[0], SImode, 0);
   operands[1] = gen_lowpart(SImode, operands[1]);
+  /* The first push has decremented the register by the time the second
+     one reads the source: compensate when the source is addressed through
+     it, e.g. a DImode spill slot pushed as a call argument.  */
+  if (MEM_P (operands[1])
+      && reg_mentioned_p (XEXP (XEXP (operands[0], 0), 0),
+			  XEXP (operands[1], 0)))
+    operands[1] = adjust_address (operands[1], SImode, 4);
 })
 
 (define_split
@@ -5061,6 +5068,11 @@
 {
   operands[0] = adjust_address(operands[0], SImode, 0);
   operands[1] = gen_highpart(SImode, operands[1]);
+  /* As above: the first store has incremented the register.  */
+  if (MEM_P (operands[1])
+      && reg_mentioned_p (XEXP (XEXP (operands[0], 0), 0),
+			  XEXP (operands[1], 0)))
+    operands[1] = adjust_address (operands[1], SImode, -4);
 })
 
 (define_split
